# ============================================================
#  Elective events — only drawn while the matching class state
#  is active (see states/states.grim, group: elective).
#  Convention: weight 16 so your class shows up most months.
# ============================================================

# ---------------- Pyromancy ----------------

@event pyro_candle
title: Light the Candle
class: routine
tone: light
track: evocation
weight: 16
art: candle
tags: class magic
scene: A dark classroom, a single candle on a stool at the far end, Professor Thorne's silhouette with folded arms.
text: Professor Thorne places a candle at the far end of the hall. "Light it. From there." The class holds its breath. Last week a boy lit his own sleeve.
> left: A careful spark
  challenge spell standard steady:
    win:
      arcana +tiny
      rel thorne +small
      say: The wick catches with a polite little flame. Thorne grunts. From him, that is applause.
    lose:
      mood -tiny
      say: Nothing. Then a wisp of smoke from your fingertips. A few people giggle.
> right: Show them real fire
  challenge spell standard+2:
    win:
      arcana +small
      renown +small
      rel thorne +tiny
      say: The candle erupts in a pillar of white flame and then settles, obedient. The room goes quiet.
    lose:
      health -small
      study evocation -small
      rel thorne -tiny
      say: The candle lights. So do the curtains. And, briefly, your eyebrows.

@event pyro_ember_heart
title: The Ember Within
class: routine
tone: light
track: evocation
weight: 16
art: flame
tags: class magic
scene: Students sitting cross-legged in a stone circle, each with a faint glow behind their ribs.
text: Today's exercise: hold a spark inside your chest and let it grow. "Fire is fed by will," says Thorne. "And by you, if you are careless." It burns. It is supposed to burn.
> left: Stop when it hurts
  health -tiny
  arcana +tiny
  mood +tiny
  say: You let the spark gutter out. Thorne says nothing. The silence is a grade.
> right: Hold it longer than anyone
  arcana +medium
  health -medium
  say: Your vision goes white at the edges. When you open your eyes, your breath is steaming and the stones around you are warm.

@event pyro_lyra_spar
title: A Challenge in Class
class: routine
tone: tense
when: met(lyra)
track: evocation
actor: lyra
weight: 14
art: flame
tags: class rival
scene: Two students facing each other across a scorched practice ring; one is a tall girl with crimson hair, flames curling around her wrists.
text: "Professor, I'd like a demonstration partner." Lyra Vaneshade points her wand at you without looking. "That one."
> left: Politely decline
  rel lyra -tiny
  mood -tiny
  say: "As expected," Lyra says, and turns away. It stings worse than a burn would.
> right: Step into the ring
  challenge combat vs lyra.arcana:
    win:
      rel lyra +medium
      renown +small
      if bond(lyra) == "none":
        bond lyra rival
      say: Your fire meets hers and holds. When Thorne calls time, Lyra is breathing hard. "Again. Next week," she says.
    lose:
      health -small
      rel lyra +small
      say: She wins in under a minute — but she looks at you afterwards like she's filing you away for later.

# ---------------- Tidecalling ----------------

@event tide_lake_lesson
title: The Lake Answers
class: story
tone: light
track: evocation
weight: 16
art: wave
tags: class magic nature
scene: Students standing waist-deep in a silver lake at dawn, ripples spiralling out from their outstretched hands.
text: Waist-deep in the freezing lake at dawn, Professor Marisol tells you to ask the water to rise. "Ask," she says. "Never demand. The lake remembers rudeness."
> left: Command it anyway
  challenge spell apprentice+ unlikely:
    win:
      arcana +small
      say: The water rises in a shivering column. Marisol raises an eyebrow. "Effective. Rude."
    lose:
      health -tiny
      say: The lake declines, and expresses its displeasure by knocking you flat.
> right: Listen first
  lore +small
  mood +small
  say: You stand still until the cold stops hurting. The lake murmurs — and for a moment you could swear it said your name.
  chance unlikely:
    flag lake_knows

@event tide_storm_drill
title: Storm Drill
class: routine
tone: light
track: evocation
weight: 16
art: rain
tags: class nature
scene: A rocky shore under black clouds, a few figures in soaked robes holding back a curtain of rain with raised hands.
text: A storm rolls over the lake and Marisol is delighted. "Perfect conditions! Hold back the rain for as long as you can." Most of the class has already fled.
> left: Shelter with the sensible ones
  mood +tiny
  say: You watch from the boathouse, dry and slightly ashamed.
> right: Stay out in it
  vigor +small
  arcana +tiny
  chance unlikely -1 if health >= 60:
    gain sick
    say: You hold the rain back for almost a minute. You also catch Lake Fever.
  else:
    say: For a full minute, the rain parts around you. Marisol whoops like a child.

@event tide_drowned_bell
title: The Drowned Bell
class: story
tone: eerie
when: not flag(bell_fragment) and seen(hs_lake_breathes)
track: evocation
weight: 12
art: bell
tags: class mystery hollowstar
scene: Murky green water, a shaft of light catching the bronze curve of an enormous bell half-buried in silt.
text: Ever since the lake held its breath in Mistveil, you listen for it. During a breathing-charm lesson you hear it: a bell, deep under the lake, tolling slow and soft. Nobody else seems to notice.
> left: Mention it to Professor Marisol
  lore +tiny
  say: Her face goes very still. "There is no bell," she says. "There hasn't been a bell for three hundred years."
  flag heard_bell
  find lead_lake_breathed
> right: Dive down to find it
  challenge feat adept- wild:
    win:
      lore +small
      flag bell_fragment
      find lead_lake_breathed
      say: Deep in the silt you find a broken piece of bronze, warm to the touch, engraved with a black star.
    lose:
      health -medium
      say: The water closes over you, dark and cold. You surface gasping, empty-handed, with the bell still ringing in your teeth.

# ---------------- Illusion ----------------

@event illusion_mirror_self
title: A Second You
class: routine
tone: light
track: illusion
weight: 16
art: mirror
tags: class magic
scene: A student facing a shimmering duplicate of themselves; the duplicate's smile is a little too wide.
text: Assignment: conjure a convincing illusion of yourself. Professor Vey circles the room. "Most students make themselves taller. Interesting, what people choose."
> left: Make it flattering
  charm +small
  mood +small
  say: Your double is radiant, confident, slightly better-looking. Vey writes something down and smiles thinly.
> right: Make it accurate
  guile +tiny
  lore +tiny
  say: Your double slouches the way you slouch and chews its lip the way you do. It is deeply unsettling. Vey awards top marks.
  study illusion +tiny

@event illusion_professor_prank
title: The Professor's Face
class: routine
tone: light
track: illusion
weight: 14
art: mask
tags: class social
scene: A student wearing a shimmering glamour of a stern old professor, classmates stifling laughter behind a door.
text: Your classmates dare you: wear a glamour of Professor Thorne and cancel tomorrow's Arcana lecture. "Nobody will know," says someone who will definitely tell.
> left: Absolutely not
  study illusion +tiny
  say: Wise. Someone else tries it the next day and spends a week scrubbing gargoyles.
> right: Do it
  alignment -tiny
  challenge deceive using charm journeyman+ wild:
    win:
      renown +medium
      mood +small
      say: "Class is cancelled," you announce in Thorne's gravel voice. The cheering is audible from three towers away.
    lose:
      gain detention
      study illusion -small
      rel thorne -small
      say: Halfway through, the glamour flickers. The real Thorne is standing in the doorway. He is not laughing.

@event illusion_dragon
title: The Courtyard Dragon
class: routine
tone: light
when: arcana >= 12
track: illusion
weight: 12
art: dragon
tags: class magic
scene: A vast translucent dragon coiled around the academy's central fountain, students frozen mid-step beneath it.
text: For your term project you must create an illusion that fools a crowd. You could make something small and flawless. Or you could put a dragon in the courtyard at lunchtime.
> left: Small and flawless
  study illusion +small
  say: A single butterfly that nobody can tell is fake. Vey taps it with her wand and it bursts into light. "Perfect."
> right: Dragon. Obviously.
  challenge spell using charm standard+1 wild:
    win:
      renown +medium
      study illusion +tiny
      say: The dragon uncurls around the fountain and yawns. Forty students scream. Vey laughs until she cries.
    lose:
      renown +small
      study illusion -small
      rel isolde -tiny
      say: The dragon is magnificent for four seconds and then sneezes into a cloud of glitter. The headmistress was eating lunch below it.

# ---------------- Practical Alchemy ----------------

@event alch_first_brew
title: Draught of Mild Courage
class: routine
tone: light
track: alchemy
weight: 16
art: cauldron
tags: class
scene: Rows of bubbling cauldrons in a low stone room, each giving off a different coloured steam.
text: The recipe is on the board: Draught of Mild Courage. Seven ingredients, three stirs clockwise, one counter-clockwise, and never — never — add the newt eye early.
> left: Follow the recipe exactly
  alchemy +tiny
  study alchemy +tiny
  say: A clear, honey-coloured brew. The professor sniffs it and nods. Safe, solid, unremarkable.
> right: Improvise a little
  challenge brew standard wild:
    win:
      alchemy +medium
      gold +small
      say: Your variant tastes like cinnamon and makes people brave enough to ask for things. A fourth-year buys the whole flask.
    lose:
      gain frog_voice
      say: You taste-test. Mistake. For the next month, everything you say comes out as a deep, wet croak.

@event alch_unstable_cauldron
title: Unstable Cauldron
class: routine
tone: tense
track: alchemy
weight: 14
art: potion
tags: class danger
scene: A cauldron shuddering on its iron legs, violet bubbles swelling over the rim, a student frozen beside it.
text: The cauldron next to yours starts to shudder. Its owner, a terrified first-year, has added the newt eye early. It is going to blow.
> left: Dive for cover
  say: The explosion paints the ceiling violet. Nobody is hurt. Everybody is purple.
> right: Try to neutralise it
  challenge brew standard+1:
    win:
      renown +small
      alchemy +small
      say: A pinch of salt, a drop of moonwater, a quick counter-stir. The bubbling dies. The first-year bursts into grateful tears.
    lose:
      health -medium
      say: The cauldron goes off in your face. You spend a week with violet eyebrows and a ringing in your ears.

@event alch_corvin_market
title: A Side Business
class: routine
tone: light
when: met(corvin)
track: alchemy
actor: corvin
weight: 12
art: bottle
tags: class money
scene: A young man leaning on a cauldron table, holding up a vial against the light with a merchant's grin.
text: Corvin turns your leftover potions over in his hands. "These would sell for real crowns in the village. I know a buyer. I take a third. Nobody needs to know they came from a classroom."
> left: Decline
  rel corvin -tiny
  say: "Your loss, saint." He tosses the vial back. You fumble it.
> right: Shake on it
  alignment -tiny
  gold +large
  rel corvin +small
  chance unlikely:
    gain detention
    study alchemy -small
    say: It goes well until a vial turns up in a professor's tea. You and Corvin share a detention and an alibi.
  else:
    say: Thirty crowns, no questions asked. Corvin winks. "Pleasure doing crime with you."

# ---------------- Divination ----------------

@event div_tea_leaves
title: Reading the Leaves
class: routine
tone: eerie
track: astromancy
weight: 16
art: cup
tags: class mystery
scene: A delicate teacup tipped on its saucer, the dregs forming a shape like a skull — or possibly a mushroom.
text: You read your partner's tea leaves. The shape at the bottom of the cup is unmistakably a skull. Your partner is looking at you hopefully.
> left: Tell the truth
  lore +small
  chance even:
    say: "A skull?" They laugh. "Professor says a skull means change." They're relieved. You aren't sure you should be.
  else:
    mood -tiny
    say: They go pale and leave early. The next day they trip down the stairs. Nothing serious. Still.
> right: Lie kindly
  mood -tiny
  charm +small
  say: "A mushroom," you say. "Means good fortune." They beam. The professor, passing behind you, says nothing at all.
> up[omen]: Foretell what it really means
  lore +small
  mood +tiny
  say: You say, out loud and quite certain, that the skull means your partner will lose a bet before Friday. They lose a bet on Thursday, to you, and are thrilled the skull wasn't worse.

@event div_next_tuesday
title: The Mirror of Next Tuesday
class: routine
tone: eerie
track: astromancy
weight: 14
art: mirror
tags: class mystery
scene: An ornate standing mirror whose reflection shows the room on a different day — the light at a different angle, a different person sitting in your chair.
text: The Mirror of Next Tuesday shows exactly what it promises. Students take turns looking. Some come away smiling. One comes away and goes straight to the infirmary.
> left: Take a look
  chance even:
    study astromancy +small
    alignment -tiny
    say: Next Tuesday you are sitting an Astromancy quiz. You memorise the questions. Is that cheating? It's at least ambiguous.
  else:
    mood -medium
    say: Next Tuesday you are crying in the rain outside the observatory. You don't know why. You spend the week dreading it.
> right: Decline
  mood +tiny
  say: "I'd rather be surprised." The professor smiles as if you have passed a different test entirely.

@event div_seraphine_vision
title: She Grabs Your Hand
class: story
tone: eerie
track: astromancy
actor: seraphine
weight: 14
art: eye
tags: class mystery hollowstar
chain: hollowstar
scene: A dreamy-eyed girl gripping a classmate's wrist across a table of crystal balls, her pupils wide and silver.
text: In the middle of crystal-gazing, Seraphine Hale seizes your wrist. Her eyes have gone silver. "The door under the lake," she whispers. "Don't let him open it. Or do. I can't see which."
> left: Pull away
  meet seraphine
  rel seraphine -tiny
  mood -tiny
  say: She blinks and lets go. "Sorry. That happens." She goes back to her crystal as if nothing occurred.
> right: Ask who she means
  meet seraphine
  rel seraphine +medium
  lore +tiny
  flag heard_prophecy
  say: "Someone cold," she says. "Someone kind." Then she shakes her head, smiles vaguely, and asks if you'd like a biscuit.

# ---------------- Artifice ----------------

@event art_clockwork_beetle
title: The Clockwork Beetle
class: routine
tone: light
track: artifice
weight: 16
art: gear
tags: class
scene: A brass beetle the size of a fist on a workbench, tiny gears visible through its translucent wing-cases.
text: Your project: a brass beetle that walks. The gears are in. The spring is wound. You could make it efficient, or you could give it a little personality.
> left: Make it efficient
  study artifice +tiny
  lore +tiny
  say: It walks in a perfect straight line until it hits a wall. Full marks.
> right: Give it personality
  mood +small
  chance unlikely:
    renown +small
    say: It escapes during the presentation and lives in the walls for a month, occasionally stealing biscuits. It becomes a minor legend.
  else:
    say: It refuses to walk unless you compliment it. The professor is torn between marking you down and asking how you did it.
> up[animate]: Animate it instead of winding it
  study artifice +tiny
  mood +tiny
  say: You skip the spring and give the beetle a want instead: to find the warmest spot on the bench. It does, and sits there, content, and nothing in the class is wound tighter or happier.

@event art_mir_collab
title: A Joint Project
class: routine
tone: light
track: artifice
actor: mir
weight: 14
art: gear
tags: class social
scene: A cluttered workbench covered in tools, sketches and one smoking teapot; a grinning student with goggles pushed up into wild hair.
text: Mir Ten drops onto the bench beside you with a sketch of something that is either a self-stirring cauldron or a small war machine. "Partners? Your hands, my brain. Or the other way round. Both, actually."
> left: Work alone
  meet mir
  study artifice +tiny
  say: "Fair," says Mir, with no hard feelings, and is immediately on fire. Not badly.
> right: Partner with Mir
  meet mir
  challenge brew standard wild:
    win:
      study artifice +small
      rel mir +medium
      say: The cauldron stirs itself, hums a tune and only threatens the professor once. Mir hugs you with oily hands.
    lose:
      health -small
      rel mir +small
      say: The prototype explodes. Mir laughs so hard they cry. "Again! We were so close!" You find you're laughing too.
> up[contraption]: Build it on the spot
  meet mir
  study artifice +tiny
  rel mir +small
  say: You don't sketch it. You ask the bits what they want to be, and they become a cauldron that stirs and occasionally salutes. Mir makes a noise you've never heard a person make. "Partners," Mir says. "Forever. Probably."

@event art_enchanted_quill
title: The Self-Writing Quill
class: routine
tone: light
track: artifice
weight: 14
art: feather
tags: class
scene: A quill writing busily on its own over a sheaf of paper while its owner sleeps on folded arms.
text: You've enchanted a quill to take dictation. It works beautifully. A thought occurs: what if it wrote your essays, too?
> left: Just use it for notes
  lore +small
  say: Your notes are flawless. Even the professor's jokes are transcribed, with a small marginal comment: "(not funny)."
> right: Let it write your essays
  alignment -tiny
  chance even:
    study artifice +small
    mood +small
    say: Your essays arrive on time, in impeccable penmanship. A little too impeccable. Nobody notices. Yet.
  else:
    study artifice -medium
    gain detention
    say: The quill develops opinions and writes a scathing review of the professor. It signs your name.

# ---------------- Beastcraft ----------------

@event beast_griffon_chick
title: Hatching Day
class: routine
tone: light
track: beastcraft
weight: 16
art: feather
tags: class nature
scene: A straw nest under a heat lamp, a cracked golden egg, and a damp fluffy griffon chick blinking at the world.
text: The griffon egg is cracking. Professor Brask whispers that the first face a chick sees, it trusts forever — or attacks forever. Hard to predict.
> left: Hang back
  lore +tiny
  say: The chick sees Brask first and bites her. She seems delighted.
> right: Offer your hand
  challenge feat apprentice+ luck:
    win:
      mood +medium
      vigor +tiny
      say: The chick peeps, nuzzles your palm and falls asleep. You are, apparently, its mother now.
    lose:
      health -small
      say: It bites. Hard. Griffon beaks are sharper than they look, and they look extremely sharp.

@event beast_manticore
title: The Manticore Is Loose
class: routine
tone: tense
track: beastcraft
weight: 12
art: paw
tags: class danger
scene: A shadowy lion-shape with a scorpion's tail prowling between the greenhouse benches, students pressed against the glass.
text: Someone left the manticore pen open. It's in the greenhouse, tail twitching, between you and the only exit.
> left: Back away slowly
  say: You edge out. Professor Brask arrives with a bucket of meat and a lullaby and the crisis is over in minutes.
> right: Try to calm it
  challenge soothe adept wild:
    win:
      renown +medium
      vigor +tiny
      say: You hum the lullaby Brask taught you. The manticore yawns, sits, and lets you scratch behind its ear. The whole class saw.
    lose:
      health -large
      gain injured
      say: The manticore does not like your humming. The tail is quicker than you are.

@event beast_familiar_call
title: Calling a Familiar
class: routine
tone: light
when: not has(familiar_fox)
track: beastcraft
weight: 12
art: fox
tags: class magic
scene: A circle of salt and candles in a forest clearing at dusk, shapes of small animals watching from the edge of the trees.
text: Brask teaches the summoning circle. "It doesn't summon," she says. "It invites. Most of the time, nothing comes. That's fine. Familiars choose you."
> left: Just watch the others
  lore +tiny
  say: A first-year is chosen by a very large toad. The toad looks smug about it.
> right: Sit in the circle
  mood +small
  flag familiar_affinity
  say: Nothing comes. But for a long moment, something at the edge of the trees watches you with eyes like embers. Then it is gone.

# ---------------- Astromancy ----------------

@event astro_comet
title: A New Comet
class: routine
tone: light
track: astromancy
weight: 16
art: star
tags: class
scene: An observatory dome open to the night, a long-tailed comet smeared across the sky, students crowded at the telescopes.
text: A comet appears that isn't in any of the charts. The observatory is in uproar. Everyone wants to be the one to name it.
> left: Sketch it carefully
  lore +small
  say: Your drawing is lovely. Someone else's name goes on the comet. You keep the drawing.
> right: Calculate its path
  challenge research standard+1:
    win:
      renown +medium
      lore +small
      say: Your math is right. The comet is named after you, or at least after a slight misspelling of you.
    lose:
      study astromancy -tiny
      say: Your calculation suggests the comet will hit the academy on Thursday. It does not. You are teased about it for weeks.

@event astro_kael_roof
title: Up All Night
class: story
tone: eerie
when: met(kael)
track: astromancy
actor: kael
weight: 14
art: moon
tags: class mystery hollowstar
chain: hollowstar
scene: A young man in a fur coat sitting alone on the observatory roof, frost on the tiles around him, staring at one spot in the stars.
text: On your way to the morning lecture you find Kael alone on the observatory roof. He has been there all night. Frost has spread across the tiles around him. He is staring at a patch of sky where there are no stars at all.
> left: Leave him be
  say: You go down to class. By evening there's a perfect circle of frost on the roof where he sat, and no Kael.
> right: Sit beside him
  rel kael +medium
  lore +tiny
  flag saw_hollow_star
  say: "There," he says, pointing at the dark. "Can you see it? A star that eats light." You look for a long time. You think you can.

@event astro_sleepless
title: Sleepless Weeks
class: routine
tone: light
track: astromancy
weight: 14
art: bed
tags: class
scene: A student asleep on an open star atlas at a library desk, a guttering candle beside them, dawn light in the window.
text: Midnight lectures, dawn homework, morning classes. You have started seeing constellations in your porridge.
> left: Skip a few lectures
  study track -tiny
  gain slacking
  health +small
  say: You sleep for fourteen hours and wake up feeling like a person.
> right: Power through
  health -small
  lore +small
  say: You learn the names of forty stars and forget the names of two friends. Temporarily.

# ---------------- Healing Arts ----------------

@event heal_first_patient
title: Your First Patient
class: routine
tone: light
track: alchemy
weight: 16
art: cross
tags: class
scene: A pale first-year sitting on an infirmary cot holding a wrist at a strange angle, a nervous student healer kneeling beside them.
text: A first-year stumbles into the practice ward with a wrist that bends the wrong way. Sister Amaranth is busy. The first-year looks at you with enormous, trusting eyes.
> left: Fetch Sister Amaranth
  study alchemy +tiny
  say: Amaranth fixes it in seconds and nods at you. "Knowing your limits is the first lesson."
> right: Heal it yourself
  challenge brew standard+1:
    win:
      alchemy +small
      renown +small
      say: The bone slides back with a soft click and a glow of warm light. The first-year tells everyone you're a genius.
    lose:
      study alchemy -small
      say: The wrist is now straight. The fingers, however, are pointing backwards. Amaranth sighs and fixes both.

@event heal_fever_ward
title: Fever in the Village
class: routine
tone: light
track: alchemy
weight: 12
art: cross
tags: class nature
scene: A crowded village hall lined with cots, lanterns hanging from the rafters, student healers moving between patients.
text: Lake Fever is spreading through the village below the academy. Sister Amaranth asks for student volunteers. It's hard, unpaid, and you might catch it.
> left: Decline
  mood -tiny
  say: You watch the volunteers board the barge in the morning. You do your homework. It feels like the wrong homework.
> right: Volunteer
  renown +tiny
  alchemy +tiny
  mood +tiny
  alignment +tiny
  chance unlikely -1 if health >= 60:
    gain sick
    say: You save lives, and catch the fever yourself. The village sends a basket of honey cakes to your sickbed.
  else:
    say: A week of long nights and cool cloths. When you leave, the baker's daughter gives you her best loaf.

@event heal_tobias_sting
title: Stung
class: windfall
tone: light
when: met(tobias) and rel(tobias) >= 0
track: alchemy
actor: tobias
weight: 12
art: flower
tags: class social
scene: A broad-shouldered boy sitting on a greenhouse bench, grimacing, holding up a hand swollen to twice its size.
text: Tobias wanders into the practice ward holding up a hand swollen like a pumpkin. "Mandrake," he says. "She didn't like my singing." He looks hopefully at you.
> left: Send him to the infirmary
  rel tobias +tiny
  say: "Right. Proper healer. Good idea." He goes, a little disappointed.
> right: Treat him yourself
  alchemy +tiny
  rel tobias +medium
  spark tobias +tiny
  say: Your hands are steady. The swelling goes down. Tobias stares at his hand, then at you. "You're really good at this," he says softly.

# ---------------- Umbral Theory ----------------

@event umbral_whisper
title: The Shadow Speaks
class: routine
tone: eerie
track: umbral
weight: 16
art: skull
tags: class mystery danger
scene: A student at a desk in a dim lecture hall, their shadow on the wall behind them turned the wrong way, leaning close to whisper.
text: In the middle of a lecture on the Nature of Absence, your shadow leans away from the lamp, toward your ear, and says your name.
> left: Banish it
  arcana +tiny
  say: You speak the warding phrase. Your shadow snaps back into place, sulking. It does not speak again. You think.
> right: Answer it
  lore +medium
  chance unlikely:
    gain umbral_curse
    say: It tells you something about death you can't unlearn. The cold starts the next morning.
  else:
    say: It tells you where a lost book is shelved in the library. It is right. You decide not to wonder how it knew.

@event umbral_bone_mouse
title: The Bone Mouse
class: routine
tone: light
track: umbral
weight: 14
art: skull
tags: class magic
scene: A tiny mouse skeleton on a silver tray, one bony paw twitching, students leaning away from it.
text: Practical exercise: animate the skeleton of a field mouse. "Purely educational," the professor says, with a smile nobody trusts.
> left: Refuse on principle
  study umbral -tiny
  mood +tiny
  say: You write a short essay on why instead. The professor reads it with surprising attention.
> right: Do the exercise
  challenge spell standard:
    win:
      arcana +medium
      study umbral +tiny
      say: The little skeleton stands up, washes its non-existent whiskers, and lies down again. Perfect control.
    lose:
      gain haunted
      say: It gets up. It does not lie down again. It follows you back to your dormitory and sits on your pillow every night.

